{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwjgSRWst2s8AvsNxZ5Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check how the panels render, and I haven't confirmed the rule's query matches 5xx documents.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has a `timestamp` field and these main fields:\n- `response`, a string holding the HTTP status code\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n- `agent`\n\nI grouped on the `.keyword` versions of the string fields.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-a7f403da Web logs overview\" has four panels, with a default range of the last 7 days:\n- Total requests (a single-number metric)\n- Requests over time (a line chart)\n- Requests by response code (a pie chart)\n- Average bytes by extension (a bar chart)\n\nIt is at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a7f403da-web-logs-overview-323e489f0fcc`.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-a7f403da 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule (`.es-query`) that runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents in the last 5 minutes have a `response.keyword` matching `5[0-9][0-9]`. The rule ID is `82cb7714-8276-428a-9cca-e62ff9af2a8e`.\n\nThe rule has no action attached, so when it fires it only shows up in Kibana's alert views and doesn't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":20403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"output_tokens":515,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"52c973bb-eab8-4523-9112-f74b1ce159e0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:47:13.